customer: young_entrepreneur
problem: bootfloppy
brief:
	The boot floppy is how Cambion got onto his computer. It carries only a Windows 95 logo: naming Cambion is too early here, and nothing points at it.

== drop-off
(neutral) Hello. Do you do business computers?
- What's your business?
	(happy) Import and export. Mostly import. Okay, mostly ideas, so far.
- We do all sorts of computers.
	(thinking) Of course you do. Anything else would have been a bad business decision.

- So, what is your problem?
- Well...
(problem) My computer won't start. It just shows a bunch of text, something about a disk.
- Did you put a floppy in?
(thinking) Just some software a guy gave me. Business stuff. Very cutting edge.
- OK, leave it with me.
(happy) Great. I'd really appreciate it if you fixed it as soon as possible. You'd really do me a solid there.
(irritated01) Time is money, you know.
- So I've heard...

== pick-up
(happy) That was quick! You sure seems to know what's essential for running a successful business!
- It was quite an easy fix actually.
- Just doing my job.
(neutral) Still! I see unleashed potential!
- Oh, really?
- What does that even mean?
(neutral) I have to run! But you should come to our business after work sometime!
- ...sure...
